WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.153 --> 00:00:02.193
- What have I come to terms with?

00:00:04.710 --> 00:00:05.543
Wow.

00:00:07.107 --> 00:00:08.190
(clears throat)

00:00:08.190 --> 00:00:10.470
The possibility, I've never been married,

00:00:10.470 --> 00:00:13.263
the possibility that I
never will find somebody.

00:00:14.910 --> 00:00:17.010
It's been developing over years

00:00:17.010 --> 00:00:18.663
because I took care of my mom,

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:22.260
sorry, before she passed,

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:24.240
and it was 14 years.

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:25.173
She had dementia.

00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:29.440
And I never knew she'd

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:31.830
survive that long.

00:00:31.830 --> 00:00:36.253
Or I didn't know, and
yeah, how that would go

00:00:36.253 --> 00:00:38.883
when I decided to become her caregiver.

00:00:39.930 --> 00:00:43.083
So, I think it was during that time

00:00:43.083 --> 00:00:46.620
that I relegated myself to the possibility

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:50.130
that I may not find somebody.

00:00:50.130 --> 00:00:54.030
And so many years went by
and she passed in December.

00:00:54.030 --> 00:00:55.413
It's now August.

00:00:56.970 --> 00:00:59.040
So, many years have gone
by that now I think,

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:01.533
okay, well, am I gonna be alone?

00:01:03.150 --> 00:01:05.553
Or, maybe I'll find
somebody, I don't know.

00:01:07.650 --> 00:01:09.483
- Probably that I'll never be happy.

00:01:10.366 --> 00:01:11.526
(bystander laughing)

00:01:11.526 --> 00:01:13.337
Don't laugh.

00:01:13.337 --> 00:01:15.503
- [Bystander] I'm so with you on that.

00:01:15.503 --> 00:01:17.730
- I think I'm just always,

00:01:17.730 --> 00:01:20.880
every day, you wake up
and you go about your day.

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:25.470
But the constant, what's
gonna make me happy?

00:01:25.470 --> 00:01:26.550
What's gonna make me happy?

00:01:26.550 --> 00:01:30.180
And even if I do things, I travel,

00:01:30.180 --> 00:01:31.013
I have my kids,

00:01:31.013 --> 00:01:33.150
I have everything I want,

00:01:33.150 --> 00:01:34.530
but I still feel unhappy.

00:01:34.530 --> 00:01:36.750
And you have a partner like my husband,

00:01:36.750 --> 00:01:39.577
he's always telling me,
"You're not gonna be happy.

00:01:39.577 --> 00:01:40.717
"Why are you doing this?

00:01:40.717 --> 00:01:41.550
"Why are you doing this?

00:01:41.550 --> 00:01:42.383
"Why do you want that?

00:01:42.383 --> 00:01:44.100
"You're still not gonna be happy".

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:45.900
And then you get the new kitchen,

00:01:45.900 --> 00:01:49.380
or you get the new plastic
surgery, you get the boobs,

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:51.540
and a month later,

00:01:51.540 --> 00:01:54.120
you're still walking around
with your face made up

00:01:54.120 --> 00:01:57.180
because I'm still unhappy,

00:01:57.180 --> 00:01:58.710
But I have everything.

00:01:58.710 --> 00:01:59.910
I'm not sick.

00:01:59.910 --> 00:02:00.840
I don't have any ailments.

00:02:00.840 --> 00:02:02.223
My family's happy.

00:02:03.420 --> 00:02:06.120
We're comfortable, but why am I unhappy?

00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:07.710
Why do I want?

00:02:07.710 --> 00:02:09.030
Why can't?

00:02:09.030 --> 00:02:11.490
What I want, I think, is unattainable.

00:02:11.490 --> 00:02:12.780
And I think that somehow,

00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:14.930
I have to learn to
create my own happiness.

00:02:16.530 --> 00:02:18.076
- [Thoraya] What's something

00:02:18.076 --> 00:02:19.770
you've finally come to terms with?

00:02:19.770 --> 00:02:21.090
- Racism.

00:02:21.090 --> 00:02:24.180
One time when me try to go to Tijuana,

00:02:24.180 --> 00:02:27.960
the border patrol told me jump the hill.

00:02:27.960 --> 00:02:30.003
It's immigration patrol.

00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:31.953
I feel really bad,

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:35.550
because I can't believe living,

00:02:35.550 --> 00:02:39.000
one line divide Mexico with US

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:40.923
and it's a lot of racism.

00:02:41.850 --> 00:02:45.330
For me, after 15 years living here,

00:02:45.330 --> 00:02:48.990
I feel comfort because every day is just,

00:02:48.990 --> 00:02:50.490
every day you see the racism.

00:02:50.490 --> 00:02:52.200
Every day is different people.

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:53.433
I work in the casino.

00:02:54.537 --> 00:02:56.100
I have with the Chinese people,

00:02:56.100 --> 00:03:01.100
African people, a lot of people
diverse in other countries.

00:03:01.110 --> 00:03:04.203
In my job I see the
racism, my coworkers too.

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:07.110
- [Thoraya] So, your coworkers are diverse

00:03:07.110 --> 00:03:08.820
and you all feel racism

00:03:08.820 --> 00:03:10.560
towards you?
- Yeah.

00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:14.010
After how many years
I'm here, I feel good.

00:03:14.010 --> 00:03:14.843
- [Thoraya] It doesn't

00:03:14.843 --> 00:03:15.970
bother you anymore?
- It doesn't

00:03:15.970 --> 00:03:16.803
bother me anymore.

00:03:16.803 --> 00:03:18.005
- [Thoraya] So, that's what you mean

00:03:18.005 --> 00:03:18.838
by you'd finally come to terms with it?

00:03:18.838 --> 00:03:19.671
- Yeah.

00:03:21.077 --> 00:03:23.613
- I don't know if this
is gonna make sense but,

00:03:24.690 --> 00:03:28.772
I came out of a cult, so I
guess I just came out of terms

00:03:28.772 --> 00:03:31.080
that even if you lose loved ones

00:03:31.080 --> 00:03:33.210
because of something that you believe,

00:03:33.210 --> 00:03:34.650
like strongly believe,

00:03:34.650 --> 00:03:39.210
and that it's not good for you,
or safe for you, it's okay.

00:03:39.210 --> 00:03:41.550
It was just literally my mom,

00:03:41.550 --> 00:03:42.780
my sisters, my brothers

00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:45.240
people that, I grew up with.

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:47.640
And it was hard on me,

00:03:47.640 --> 00:03:49.680
but I came to terms with it already.

00:03:49.680 --> 00:03:51.360
My kids were born and raised in there,

00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:53.430
but I gave them the choice.

00:03:53.430 --> 00:03:54.450
I never had the choice.

00:03:54.450 --> 00:03:57.390
I was forced into it and I left at 40,

00:03:57.390 --> 00:04:02.193
I'm 45 and I feel that I'm
barely learning how to live.

00:04:03.489 --> 00:04:04.322
Yeah.

00:04:04.322 --> 00:04:05.403
Yeah.

00:04:06.780 --> 00:04:10.443
- I've come to terms
that I'm an alcoholic.

00:04:13.909 --> 00:04:17.250
I went to a meeting this
morning, an AA meeting

00:04:17.250 --> 00:04:22.250
and I spilled out my heart
in front of all these guys.

00:04:23.370 --> 00:04:24.203
And,

00:04:26.850 --> 00:04:27.683
I don't,

00:04:29.250 --> 00:04:32.610
I'm not 100% convinced that I'm alcoholic.

00:04:32.610 --> 00:04:34.470
I don't think I ever will be,

00:04:34.470 --> 00:04:39.240
but I'm closer to that reality

00:04:39.240 --> 00:04:40.893
than I was yesterday.

00:04:42.420 --> 00:04:43.293
And,

00:04:45.720 --> 00:04:47.790
I'm at peace with that, you know?

00:04:47.790 --> 00:04:48.623
And,

00:04:51.780 --> 00:04:56.223
it's a peace that I
can't put my finger on.

00:04:57.270 --> 00:04:58.683
It's something sublime.

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:03.150
- Something I finally come to terms with

00:05:03.150 --> 00:05:07.650
is probably just looks,
face, body, everything.

00:05:07.650 --> 00:05:10.530
I guess accepting that it's gonna change.

00:05:10.530 --> 00:05:12.690
I'm gonna get skinnier and bigger,

00:05:12.690 --> 00:05:16.500
and I'm gonna get older

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:18.810
and my hair's gonna get frizzier

00:05:18.810 --> 00:05:21.900
maybe deader, stuff like that.

00:05:21.900 --> 00:05:25.290
And I guess I finally
come to terms with that.

00:05:25.290 --> 00:05:27.810
None of that really matters at all.

00:05:27.810 --> 00:05:32.810
I have a lot of scars
and big pores and things,

00:05:33.330 --> 00:05:34.860
that are never gonna change,

00:05:34.860 --> 00:05:38.850
but that doesn't affect anything at all.

00:05:38.850 --> 00:05:42.630
So, I guess I finally come
to terms with that I'm more.

00:05:42.630 --> 00:05:44.100
That I'm more than what I look like.

00:05:44.100 --> 00:05:47.103
My soul is what's really
roaming this earth.

00:05:48.450 --> 00:05:50.750
- Probably that not
everybody's gonna like me.

00:05:51.608 --> 00:05:52.590
Yeah.
- [Thoraya] And what made you

00:05:52.590 --> 00:05:54.628
come to terms with that?

00:05:54.628 --> 00:05:55.560
- School.

00:05:55.560 --> 00:05:57.750
I don't have friends, but it's fine.

00:05:57.750 --> 00:05:59.610
I have family and stuff
like that and my boyfriend,

00:05:59.610 --> 00:06:01.076
so that's good.

00:06:01.076 --> 00:06:01.909
But yeah.

00:06:01.909 --> 00:06:02.742
- [Thoraya] What's something

00:06:02.742 --> 00:06:04.143
you've finally come to terms with?

00:06:05.310 --> 00:06:07.320
- Losing my vision.

00:06:07.320 --> 00:06:11.070
I had a stroke and the blood
clot went behind my eye

00:06:11.070 --> 00:06:12.480
instead of to my brain.

00:06:12.480 --> 00:06:16.320
So, maybe I'm lucky, but I lost vision.

00:06:16.320 --> 00:06:19.220
Acceptance is always something
that makes you feel better.

00:06:21.450 --> 00:06:23.490
And it turned out to be okay.

00:06:23.490 --> 00:06:25.080
Everything's fine.

00:06:25.080 --> 00:06:25.913
- Nothing.

00:06:25.913 --> 00:06:27.480
I'm still in denial.

00:06:27.480 --> 00:06:28.590
Yup.

00:06:28.590 --> 00:06:30.290
I don't like thinking about stuff.

00:06:31.320 --> 00:06:34.084
It'll take care of its own in the future.

00:06:34.084 --> 00:06:35.100
I don't know.

00:06:35.100 --> 00:06:36.540
I don't like to think about the future.

00:06:36.540 --> 00:06:38.100
It makes me very anxious.

00:06:38.100 --> 00:06:40.890
Thinking of failure for
me is just like a no go.

00:06:40.890 --> 00:06:41.760
I'm always positive.

00:06:41.760 --> 00:06:43.860
I always try to stay positive,

00:06:43.860 --> 00:06:47.670
so I haven't come to terms with anything.

00:06:47.670 --> 00:06:49.503
It'll always work out eventually.

00:06:52.873 --> 00:06:56.940
(people chattering indistinctly)

00:06:56.940 --> 00:06:58.440
- Yeah, you know what?

00:06:58.440 --> 00:07:00.617
In a personal matter,
a very personal matter,

00:07:00.617 --> 00:07:04.920
I have a 20 year old
daughter that's in school

00:07:04.920 --> 00:07:09.420
and I thought we were very,
very, very close to each other

00:07:09.420 --> 00:07:10.890
and she went away to college.

00:07:10.890 --> 00:07:12.330
And I never hear from her.

00:07:12.330 --> 00:07:13.773
I just never do.

00:07:14.910 --> 00:07:16.560
I've come to terms with that,

00:07:16.560 --> 00:07:19.140
realizing that I'm a father

00:07:19.140 --> 00:07:23.100
and daughters and sons like
me when I was 20 years old,

00:07:23.100 --> 00:07:24.150
I would go to my mother.

00:07:24.150 --> 00:07:26.100
I would never talk to my father,

00:07:26.100 --> 00:07:28.050
like I would talk to my mother.

00:07:28.050 --> 00:07:29.853
And so it's just part of,

00:07:31.230 --> 00:07:33.360
I think it might be part of human nature,

00:07:33.360 --> 00:07:35.610
or part of the family dynamic,

00:07:35.610 --> 00:07:37.983
but it took me a while to,

00:07:39.150 --> 00:07:41.820
like I had to ask a lot
of people about that,

00:07:41.820 --> 00:07:43.563
in order to come to terms with it.

00:07:45.570 --> 00:07:47.020
- That I lie to myself a lot.

00:07:48.480 --> 00:07:50.610
Yeah, I pretend that I do certain things

00:07:50.610 --> 00:07:51.930
because I like to do them,

00:07:51.930 --> 00:07:54.990
but actually it's just because my friends,

00:07:54.990 --> 00:07:57.273
or like the group that surrounds me,

00:07:58.290 --> 00:08:00.060
consider them that they are right.

00:08:00.060 --> 00:08:01.710
But I think sometimes they're not.

00:08:01.710 --> 00:08:06.710
So, it's more like just to fit, you know?

00:08:06.780 --> 00:08:07.613
Yeah.

00:08:08.880 --> 00:08:12.210
- I think recently I've
come to terms with the fact

00:08:12.210 --> 00:08:17.010
that I am shy and more antisocial

00:08:17.010 --> 00:08:19.233
and introverted.

00:08:20.520 --> 00:08:25.410
And that I don't need to
always put myself out there

00:08:25.410 --> 00:08:28.920
and put myself in more
uncomfortable situations,

00:08:28.920 --> 00:08:31.593
just to fit in and be more extroverted.

00:08:34.770 --> 00:08:37.590
- Okay, I recently just
went through a breakup,

00:08:37.590 --> 00:08:38.730
like a few days ago.

00:08:38.730 --> 00:08:39.999
I'm shaking.

00:08:39.999 --> 00:08:40.832
(speaker laughs)

00:08:40.832 --> 00:08:41.940
It's okay to let people go.

00:08:41.940 --> 00:08:44.910
To let yourself find
happiness and to grow,

00:08:44.910 --> 00:08:46.110
you gotta let people go.

00:08:47.100 --> 00:08:47.933
Yeah.

00:08:47.933 --> 00:08:49.487
That's the best it's gonna get.

00:08:49.487 --> 00:08:50.320
(speaker laughs)

00:08:50.320 --> 00:08:52.470
- I'm 56 years old now

00:08:52.470 --> 00:08:56.400
and I realized suddenly like last year,

00:08:56.400 --> 00:09:00.037
that my very good friends
are not very good friends.

00:09:00.037 --> 00:09:02.400
I thought I would never accepted it.

00:09:02.400 --> 00:09:03.780
I was so angry.

00:09:03.780 --> 00:09:06.450
I was losing all my, it's like a tree.

00:09:06.450 --> 00:09:10.020
You are losing your feet, or your branch.

00:09:10.020 --> 00:09:10.853
I don't know.

00:09:10.853 --> 00:09:13.590
But now that I realize

00:09:13.590 --> 00:09:17.790
and that I accepted it,
honestly, I feel so good

00:09:17.790 --> 00:09:22.320
but to wait 50, at 56 to do
that, I think it's a shame.

00:09:22.320 --> 00:09:24.060
I should have done it before.

00:09:24.060 --> 00:09:25.680
This is it.

00:09:25.680 --> 00:09:27.603
- I think the finality of life.

00:09:28.860 --> 00:09:31.650
That you can't have life
without it having an end.

00:09:31.650 --> 00:09:36.090
And at this age, I'm about to turn 88

00:09:36.090 --> 00:09:39.750
and I think I've come to terms pretty much

00:09:39.750 --> 00:09:44.550
with the finality of life and its ending.

00:09:44.550 --> 00:09:47.860
I'm not so crazy about
the process of ending

00:09:48.704 --> 00:09:50.183
'cause it's not too comfortable,

00:09:51.190 --> 00:09:55.923
but I'm happy with life
and I'm okay with its end.

00:09:57.000 --> 00:09:59.190
- I've finally come to terms with the fact

00:09:59.190 --> 00:10:01.410
that I'm not always right

00:10:01.410 --> 00:10:04.380
and I often have to stop and think,

00:10:04.380 --> 00:10:05.730
is this one of those moments?

00:10:05.730 --> 00:10:09.300
I have already raised my daughter,

00:10:09.300 --> 00:10:13.140
and started over by
adopting two little ones.

00:10:13.140 --> 00:10:18.140
So, I kinda got a second
chance to not be right.

00:10:18.480 --> 00:10:19.313
It feels good.

00:10:20.610 --> 00:10:21.690
- Okay, I think something

00:10:21.690 --> 00:10:25.050
that I have come to terms with finally,

00:10:25.050 --> 00:10:28.200
is that very few people in this world

00:10:28.200 --> 00:10:30.150
truly care about you.

00:10:30.150 --> 00:10:33.030
I think that we go
through life growing up,

00:10:33.030 --> 00:10:34.680
being assisted in a lot of things

00:10:34.680 --> 00:10:37.770
and we mistake that for
people actually caring,

00:10:37.770 --> 00:10:39.510
about what we have to say,

00:10:39.510 --> 00:10:41.400
or about just us in general.

00:10:41.400 --> 00:10:42.870
But then when you become an adult,

00:10:42.870 --> 00:10:45.300
I think you realize that
that's not really the case.

00:10:45.300 --> 00:10:47.250
It was all just to help you get here.

00:10:47.250 --> 00:10:48.780
And now that you, I don't know,

00:10:48.780 --> 00:10:50.130
now that you're fully grown

00:10:50.130 --> 00:10:52.560
you realize, well I think
you got your parents

00:10:52.560 --> 00:10:54.270
if you're lucky and you got your siblings,

00:10:54.270 --> 00:10:55.740
also if you're lucky.

00:10:55.740 --> 00:10:58.230
Beyond that, if you have
more people than that,

00:10:58.230 --> 00:11:00.150
who like truly do care about you,

00:11:00.150 --> 00:11:02.700
like I said you can consider
yourself very lucky.

00:11:02.700 --> 00:11:04.600
Coming to terms with that wasn't easy,

00:11:06.720 --> 00:11:08.280
but yeah, I find it to be true.

00:11:08.280 --> 00:11:09.600
- [Thoraya] I want you to reverse that.

00:11:09.600 --> 00:11:11.490
Do you feel that from your side too?

00:11:11.490 --> 00:11:14.640
Do you think, do you only
care about your siblings,

00:11:14.640 --> 00:11:17.463
or your parents and very few friends?

00:11:22.080 --> 00:11:23.040
- Yes.

00:11:23.040 --> 00:11:25.653
I think people are centric.

00:11:26.732 --> 00:11:28.050
I wouldn't describe humans as selfish.

00:11:28.050 --> 00:11:29.940
I would describe them as centric,

00:11:29.940 --> 00:11:32.640
in that your needs come first

00:11:32.640 --> 00:11:35.040
and then once your needs are met,

00:11:35.040 --> 00:11:36.420
then you start thinking about the needs

00:11:36.420 --> 00:11:37.920
of people who are close to you.

00:11:37.920 --> 00:11:39.060
And then beyond that,

00:11:39.060 --> 00:11:42.030
I think your capacity
to care about strangers,

00:11:42.030 --> 00:11:44.580
is much more limited than
we'd all like to believe.

00:11:46.290 --> 00:11:47.123
- Hi everyone.

00:11:47.123 --> 00:11:48.210
Thank you for watching.

00:11:48.210 --> 00:11:49.830
I'll be posting bonus footage

00:11:49.830 --> 00:11:51.750
from this episode on my Patreon.

00:11:51.750 --> 00:11:55.110
That means more answers and
extended cuts of each answer.

00:11:55.110 --> 00:11:56.790
If you wanna see it, you can sign up.

00:11:56.790 --> 00:11:58.440
I'll have it linked in my description

00:11:58.440 --> 00:11:59.700
and if I ever do follow-ups

00:11:59.700 --> 00:12:01.350
on the people you see in this episode,

00:12:01.350 --> 00:12:03.360
that'll be on my Patreon as well.

00:12:03.360 --> 00:12:04.680
Thank you guys for watching.

00:12:04.680 --> 00:12:07.600
I love you all and I'll see you next time.

00:12:07.600 --> 00:12:10.183
(gentle music)

